# 4-bit Register

## Goal

Learn how to implement an 4-bit register in Verilog and understand how multiple D Flip-Flops work together to store binary data.

## Concepts Learned

- register
- sequential logic
- clock
- reset
- always block
- posedge
- vector signals
- data storage

## Truth Table

| Reset | Clock  | D[7:0] | Q[7:0] (Next) |
|--------|--------|--------|---------------|
| 1      | Rising Edge | XXXXXXXX | 00000000 |
| 0      | Rising Edge | Data     | Data     |
| 0      | No Edge     | XXXXXXXX | Pr Value |

> **↑** = Rising edge of the clock  
> **X** = Don't care

